response_comment:
Two follow-ups. Pushed to focus-ring-v1 (#48743).

1. Box-shadow precedence. A correction to what I said before.

Earlier I noted the component's own focus box-shadow wins over `theme.focusVisible`, and called it intentional.
Reversed that for the three components that animate their own focus box-shadow: contained `Button`, `Fab`, and `Slider` (its color halo).
Each declares that box-shadow after the `ButtonBase`/root ring in source order.
So a customized `theme.focusVisible` box-shadow was losing the cascade.
Now they re-assert `theme.focusVisible` in the same block.
So a custom box-shadow wins over the component's default focus shadow.
The curated outline-only default is unaffected — no box-shadow key, so the elevation/halo stays.
`disableElevation` Button keeps its explicit no-shadow.

2. New public export: `focusVisibleVars` from `@mui/material/styles`.

The inset mechanism uses private custom properties, `--_focusVisible-offset` and `--_focusVisible-behavior`.
These are emitted regardless of the `cssVariables` option — they are component-level private vars, not theme vars.
So if a user wants to customize `outlineOffset` or box-shadow and keep the per-component inset behavior, they have to reference these private vars.
Asking users to hardcode a `--_` private var name is not good.
So I exposed them as a stable handle:

```ts
import { createTheme, focusVisibleVars } from '@mui/material/styles';

