I don't see the why you want to have the `groupBy` prop conditional i.e initially `undefined`. If `groupBy` is always provided, then `useAutocomplete` produces grouped option objects from the start and the cached options is consistently grouped.

The issue is that VerticalLinearStepper shares one `continueButtonRef` and one `backButtonRef` across buttons inside repeated StepContent instances, then focuses them in an effect: https://github.com/mui/material-ui/blob/40f5a12809d1153e5b102f359464560b7187ae3c/docs/data/material/components/steppers/VerticalLinearStepper.tsx#L53

The transition component change caused `StepContent` with `unmountOnExit` to have its button content unmounted or not yet remounted when the demo’s useEffect tries to `focus()` it

The issue can probably be fixed in the demo by using an array of refs for button refs instead:

```tsx
<Button
  variant="contained"
  onClick={handleNext}
  sx={{ mt: 1, mr: 1 }}
  ref={(element) => {
    continueButtonRefs.current[index] = element;
  }}
>
  {index === steps.length - 1 ? 'Finish' : 'Continue'}
</Button>
```

then only focus after it has mounted:

```ts
const previousActiveStepRef = React.useRef(activeStep);
const continueButtonRefs = React.useRef<Array<HTMLButtonElement | null>>([]);
const backButtonRefs = React.useRef<Array<HTMLButtonElement | null>>([]);
const resetButtonRef = React.useRef<HTMLButtonElement>(null);

React.useEffect(() => {
  const previousActiveStep = previousActiveStepRef.current;
  previousActiveStepRef.current = activeStep;

  const timeoutId = setTimeout(() => {
    if (previousActiveStep < activeStep) {
      if (activeStep === steps.length) {
        resetButtonRef.current?.focus();
      } else {
        continueButtonRefs.current[activeStep]?.focus();
      }
      return;
    }

    if (activeStep === 0) {
      continueButtonRefs.current[activeStep]?.focus();
      return;
    }

    backButtonRefs.current[activeStep]?.focus();
  });

  return () => clearTimeout(timeoutId);
}, [activeStep]);
```

A temporary workaround we are using to bypass this is to update our `vitest.config.ts`:

