response_comment:
@olivier-lxo Sorry, I didn't understand your issue. The `padding: 8` is not a sx prop so it will generate `padding: 8px`, not `64px`, which is correct. 

The statement "It adds support for the sx prop" means it can be used like this:
```tsx
export default function BasicUsage() {
  return <MyComponent sx={{ margin: 8 }}>Styled div</MyComponent>;
}

```

@ZeeshanTamboli thank you, I now understand that this is not how it works but I think that a short warning notice at the on the `styled` HOC that numbers will be interpreted as pixel values would help prevent misunderstandings. 

The current "basic usage" example uses numbers for padding and border radius without any notice on what unit this will result in. 
As this is a `@mui/system` component and and the docs say that "It uses a default theme if no theme is available" and that "It adds support for the the sx prop", one could expect these to be spacing values instead of pixel values (at least so did I).

A short code comment would probably be enough to help understand the difference. For example:

```javascript
import { styled } from '@mui/system';

const MyComponent = styled('div')({
  color: 'darkslategray',
  backgroundColor: 'aliceblue',
  padding: 8, // will be converted to `8px`
  borderRadius: 4, // will be converted to `4px`
});

export default function BasicUsage() {
  return (
    <MyComponent 
      sx={{
        padding: 1 // MUI spacing. `8px` for default value
      }}>
      Styled div
    </MyComponent>
  );
}
```

This looks like a docs bug in the Tailwind v4 theme snippet: https://mui.com/material-ui/integrations/tailwindcss/tailwindcss-v4/#extend-material-ui-classes.
`palette.text.secondary` includes alpha, but the docs currently map it through `--mui-palette-text-secondaryChannel`, so `text-text-secondary` becomes opaque.
We should map text colors to the full CSS vars instead:
```css
--color-text-primary: var(--mui-palette-text-primary);
--color-text-secondary: var(--mui-palette-text-secondary);
--color-text-disabled: var(--mui-palette-text-disabled);
```
We should also update vars for solid palette colors and directly use the theme palette vars and not use the `*Channel` tokens.

