I don't think Material UI will support tiny size out-of-the-box because it means producing larger bundle size of CSS by default.
3 sizes should be enough for typical application.

Material UI already support extending sizes. Here is an example to add `tiny` size to the Button:

```ts
declare module '@mui/material/Button' {
  interface ButtonPropsSizeOverrides {
    tiny: true;
  }
}

createTheme({
  components: {
    MuiButton: {
      styleOverrides: {
        root: ({ theme }) => ({
          variants: [
            {
              props: {
                size: 'tiny',
                variant: 'text',
              },
              style: {
                padding: '2px 4px', // small: 4px 5px
                fontSize: theme.typography.pxToRem(12), // small: 13
              },
            },
            {
              props: {
                size: 'tiny',
                variant: 'outlined',
              },
              style: {
                padding: '2px 8px', // small: 3px 9px
                fontSize: theme.typography.pxToRem(12), // small: 13
              },
            },
            {
              props: {
                size: 'tiny',
                variant: 'contained',
              },
              style: {
                padding: '2px 8px', // small: 4px 10px
                fontSize: theme.typography.pxToRem(12), // small: 13
              },
            },
          ],
        }),
      },
    },
  }
})
```

Note: I am working on a documentation guide to add `tiny` size that you can copy paste all of the components customization.

